e mounting pattern and socket, which are unaffected","Actual HAT revision stays unresolved (Q-07); socket depth is schematic and is not a seating height. The socket and header touch at one interface plane by authored dimensions only","A declared approximate-height gap between the HAT and a standoff reflects stock height differences in authored proxies, not a measured clearance","No thread engagement, torque, fit or installation sweep is claimed","The motor proxy has no mounting bores or thread detail: each screw passes through the gearbox as a declared omitted-bore proxy overlap bounded by the screw's own shank volume, not an engagement or fit","The motor's two mounting-hole positions are not modelled; the gearbox is placed from its output shaft and flange face, and screw paths are taken from the traced Plate A flange holes","Plate A flange hole positions are photo-traced approximations; the 2 mm thickness is probable, not measured","Motor wires and leads are zero-solid schematic and are not routed; no electrical, torque or retention claim","Spring washer opening roll and nut hex roll about the screw axis are deterministic presentation gauges, not measured orientations"],"status":"COMPLETE","stepId":"PX-V40-STEP-05","track":"instructional-only","unit":"mm","variantId":"rpi-zero-2-w","zeroSolidInstanceIds":["PX-V40-INS-RIBBON-FPC-001"]}
